    "Staffing Contract Template:Sample Master Services Agreement": {
      "name": "Sample Master Services Agreement",
      "kind": "Master Services Agreement",
      "active": 1,
      "document_title": "Master Services Agreement",
      "body": "> **Sample text.** Replace this template with the agreement approved by your attorney before sending it to clients.\n\nThis Master Services Agreement (the \"Agreement\") is entered into on {{today}} between **{{company.name}}** (\"Company\"), {{company.address}}, and **{{client.company_name}}** (\"Client\"), {{client.address}}.\n\n## 1. Services\n\nCompany will provide temporary personnel and related workforce services (the \"Services\") at the Client sites and in the positions described in each Rate Schedule signed by the parties. Each Rate Schedule is part of this Agreement.\n\n## 2. Personnel\n\nAll personnel assigned to Client are employees of Company. Company is responsible for their recruitment, screening, wages, payroll taxes, workers' compensation insurance and benefits required by law. Client directs the daily work at its sites and will not ask personnel to perform tasks outside their assigned position without Company's written approval.\n\n## 3. Client responsibilities\n\nClient will provide a safe workplace, site-specific training and the equipment needed for the work, comply with applicable safety laws, and confirm hours worked when asked by Company.\n\n## 4. Fees and payment\n\nClient will pay the hourly rates set in the applicable Rate Schedule for all hours worked. Overtime is billed at the overtime rate shown there. Company invoices weekly and payment is due on **{{client.payment_terms}}** terms. Late balances may accrue interest as permitted by law.\n\n## 5. Direct hire\n\nIf Client hires a person assigned by Company within 12 months after the person's last assignment, Client will pay Company a conversion fee equal to 20% of the person's first-year base wages, unless the person has worked 520 hours for Client through Company.\n\n## 6. Insurance\n\nEach party will keep general liability insurance and, for Company, workers' compensation insurance as required by law, and will provide certificates on request.\n\n## 7. Term and termination\n\nThis Agreement starts on the date it is signed and continues until terminated by either party with 30 days' written notice. Either party may terminate immediately for a material breach not cured within 10 days of written notice. Client pays for all Services provided up to the termination date.\n\n## 8. Limitation of liability\n\nNeither party is liable for indirect, incidental or consequential damages. Company is not responsible for losses arising from Client's instructions, vehicles or equipment beyond the limits of its insurance.\n\n## 9. General\n\nThis Agreement is governed by the laws of the State of Georgia. It is the entire agreement between the parties regarding the Services and may be amended only in writing, including by electronic signature."
    },
    "Staffing Contract Template:Sample Rate Schedule": {
      "name": "Sample Rate Schedule",
      "kind": "Rate Schedule",
      "active": 1,
      "document_title": "Rate Schedule",
      "body": "> **Sample text.** Replace this template with the version approved by your attorney before sending it to clients.\n\nThis Rate Schedule **{{agreement.name}}** is issued under the Master Services Agreement between **{{company.name}}** (\"Company\") and **{{client.company_name}}** (\"Client\").\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Site | {{agreement.site}} |\n| Effective from | {{agreement.valid_from}} |\n| Effective until | {{agreement.valid_to}} |\n| Payment terms | {{client.payment_terms}} |\n| Overtime | {{agreement.overtime_multiplier}} × the hourly rate, for hours over 40 per worker per week |\n\n## Rates\n\n{{rates_table}}\n\nRates are per hour worked by each assigned worker and include wages, payroll taxes, workers' compensation and Company's fee. Hours are recorded through Company's attendance system and summarized in weekly invoices.\n\nChanges to the positions or rates in this schedule require a new Rate Schedule signed by both parties."
    },
